{"units": [{"id": "mythos-quote8", "translation": "And it is necessary to address her with all words of greeting."}, {"id": "mythos-quote9", "translation": "I will speak a word to you."}, {"id": "mythos-quote10", "translation": "Do not speak a lengthy word, but a concise one."}, {"id": "mythos-quote11", "translation": "And pierce the word through the ears."}, {"id": "mythos-quote12", "translation": "The word is simple."}, {"id": "mythos-quote13", "translation": "Having enchanting words."}, {"id": "mythos-quote14", "translation": "Your word."}, {"id": "mythos-quote15", "translation": "I praise the words of these prayers."}, {"id": "mythos-quote16", "translation": "The word is short and clear."}, {"id": "mythos-quote17", "translation": "May a word of enchantment come from the word."}, {"id": "mythos-quote18", "translation": "An old man's word speaks these things."}, {"id": "mythos-quote19", "translation": "As is the fame of the Libyan words."}, {"id": "mythos-quote20", "translation": "For you will hear the whole word, Darius, in a brief speech."}, {"id": "mythos-quote21", "translation": "Share in this new word."}, {"id": "mythos-quote22", "translation": "When he learns the word."}, {"id": "mythos-quote23", "translation": "The land has been shaken by deed and no longer by word."}, {"id": "mythos-word1", "translation": "deed"}, {"id": "mythos-word2", "translation": "word, speech"}, {"id": "mythos-word3", "translation": "deed"}, {"id": "mythos-word4", "translation": "word, speech"}, {"id": "muthousthai-orth1", "translation": "to be spoken of"}, {"id": "muthousthai-note1", "translation": "Ag. 1368 corrupted from θυμοῦσθαι [to be angry]. See θυμόομαι."}, {"id": "muthousthai-word1", "translation": "to be angry"}, {"id": "muthousthai-word2", "translation": "to be angry"}, {"id": "mykaomai-orth1", "translation": "to low, bellow"}, {"id": "mykaomai-def1", "translation": "to low, bellow"}, {"id": "mykaomai-quote1", "translation": "About Io changed into a cow: on lofty rocks, where trusting in her strength she lows, telling the herdsman her toils."}, {"id": "myketesmos-orth1", "translation": "lowing, bellowing"}, {"id": "myketesmos-def1", "translation": "lowing, bellowing"}, {"id": "myketesmos-quote1", "translation": "Where the seat of Adrasteia and Ida are conspicuous with the lowings and roarings of sheep."}, {"id": "mykema-orth1", "translation": "lowing, bellowing"}, {"id": "mykema-def1", "translation": "lowing, bellowing"}, {"id": "mykema-quote1", "translation": "Improperly of thunder, Pr. 1062: the harsh bellowing of thunder."}, {"id": "myconos-orth1", "translation": "Myconos"}, {"id": "myconos-def1", "translation": "Myconos, an island, one of the Cyclades"}, {"id": "mukterocompos-orth1", "translation": "snorting through the nostrils"}, {"id": "mukterocompos-def1", "translation": "snorting through the nostrils"}, {"id": "mukterocompos-quote1", "translation": "Filled with snorting breaths, i.e. with breath that, emitted through the nostrils, produces a boastful sound, as Blomfield interprets. After Aeschylus, Constantine Manasses used this word."}, {"id": "mylasos-orth1", "translation": "Mylasus"}, {"id": "mylasos-def1", "translation": "Mylasus"}, {"id": "myraina-orth1", "translation": "moray eel"}, {"id": "myraina-def1", "translation": "moray eel"}, {"id": "myraina-quote1", "translation": "It was a moray eel or a viper."}, {"id": "mureros-orth1", "translation": "for ointment, containing ointment"}, {"id": "mureros-def1", "translation": "for ointment, containing ointment"}, {"id": "mureros-quote1", "translation": "Apart from the vessels for ointment."}, {"id": "myrias-orth1", "translation": "ten thousand, countless"}, {"id": "myrias-def1", "translation": "the number ten thousand, countless"}, {"id": "myrias-quote1", "translation": "A very dense (thus Franzius for γάρ φύστις) myriad of men has perished."}, {"id": "myrietes-orth1", "translation": "of ten thousand years, immense"}, {"id": "myrietes-def1", "translation": "embracing the number of ten thousand (i.e. immense) years"}, {"id": "myrietes-quote1", "translation": "I will toil for a time of ten thousand years."}, {"id": "myriontarchos-orth1", "translation": "commander of ten thousand"}, {"id": "myriontarchos-def1", "translation": "commander of ten thousand"}, {"id": "myriontarchos-quote1", "translation": "Matalus, commander of ten thousand."}, {"id": "myriontarchos-quote2", "translation": "But at 994: Mardon, commander of ten thousand men, Xanthis, where the meter requires μυριοταγόν, which I have restored. For it is absurd to pronounce μυριόνταρχον with four syllables."}, {"id": "myrios-orth1", "translation": "countless, innumerable"}, {"id": "myrios-def1", "translation": "properly said of the number ten thousand, very often has the meaning of countless"}, {"id": "myrios-quote1", "translation": "Judge of ten thousand horses."}, {"id": "myrios-quote2", "translation": "Ten thousand, ten thousand, the counter."}, {"id": "myrios-quote3", "translation": "Bent by countless sufferings and miseries."}, {"id": "myrios-quote4", "translation": "Worn down by countless toils."}, {"id": "myriopos-orth1", "translation": "with countless eyes"}, {"id": "myriopos-def1", "translation": "furnished with ten thousand, i.e. countless, eyes"}, {"id": "myriopos-quote1", "translation": "Seeing the many-eyed herdsman."}, {"id": "myrmex-orth1", "translation": "ant"}, {"id": "myrmex-def1", "translation": "ant"}, {"id": "myrmex-quote1", "translation": "Like light ants."}, {"id": "myrmidones-orth1", "translation": "Myrmidons"}, {"id": "myrmidones-def1", "translation": "was the title of a play of Aeschylus (fr. 128-140)."}, {"id": "myron-orth1", "translation": "ointment, perfume"}, {"id": "myron-def1", "translation": "ointment, perfume"}, {"id": "myron-quote1", "translation": "Your baccaris and perfumes."}, {"id": "mys-orth1", "translation": "mussel"}, {"id": "mys-def1", "translation": "mussel or muscle"}, {"id": "mys-quote1", "translation": "Shellfish, mussels, and oysters."}, {"id": "mysagma-orth1", "translation": "pollution, defilement"}, {"id": "mysagma-def1", "translation": "stain, defilement"}, {"id": "mysagma-quote1", "translation": "And to say it is easy, a pollution somehow."}, {"id": "mysios-orth1", "translation": "Mysian"}, {"id": "mysios-def1", "translation": "Mysian"}, {"id": "mysios-quote1", "translation": "And Seisames the Mysian."}, {"id": "mysios-quote2", "translation": "And I will mount the Mysian. Where the scholiast says: For the Mysians and Phrygians are especially mournful. And similarly Eustathius on Dionysius Periegetes 221. Fr. 141: Mysian streams."}, {"id": "mysos-orth1", "translation": "Mysian"}, {"id": "mysos-def1", "translation": "Mysian"}]}